cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Retention Advantage Ratio: A Time-Indexed Framework for Evaluating Distributed Practice Efficiency"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wish
    given-names: Michael J.
    email: michaelj.wish@gmail.com
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23484598
repository-code: "https://github.com/mike8685/retention-advantage-ratio"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >-
  Code and manuscript for the retention advantage ratio R(t) = P_distributed(t) / P_blocked(t),
  analyzed on the log scale. Under a power law of forgetting with a shared time scale, the
  log-ratio separates exactly into an initial-strength term and a decay-rate term. The framework
  is applied to the retention surface fitted by Cepeda et al. (2008), with model values compared
  against data-implied values and a proposed reporting standard.
keywords:
  - spacing effect
  - distributed practice
  - retention interval
  - desirable difficulties
  - log response ratio
